---
term: Act of commission
section: life-cycle
order: 30
definition: The creation of a new corporation by a [[parent corporation]], which writes the new charter's purpose and delegates authority to it.
example: A national health corporation commissions a regional pandemic-preparedness corporation. The commission sets its budget, gives it jurisdiction over medical stockpiles, and schedules a review in five years.
seeAlso:
  - charter-formation
  - voluntary-association
  - independent-formation
---
Commission is one of three ways a charter can originate. It suits cases where a parent needs a dedicated body to pursue part of its own objective.
